<title>UK: Jardine Fleming ex-chairman quits HK Land.</title>
<headline>Jardine Fleming ex-chairman quits HK Land.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alan Smith, who resigned as chairman of fund managers Jardine Fleming Holdings Ltd after a trading scandal in September, stepped down as a director of property company Hongkong Land Holdings Ltd on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The announcement was made in a brief statement by Jardine Matheson Ltd to the London stock exchange, where Hongkong Land and other affiliated Jardine companies have secondary listings.</p>
<p>Jardine Fleming is a joint venture between Jardine Matheson and privately-owned British investment bank Robert Fleming.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
